WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:08.000
Observed queries interact with blue FP16 key tiles
while the keys remain in the hot cache.

00:08.000 --> 00:17.500
The same query produces different attention with
FP16 keys and reconstructed 2-bit keys.

00:17.500 --> 00:22.000
QTrace estimates sensitivity to quantization.
H_d accumulates original attention times squared query activations / d.

00:22.000 --> 00:28.000
Each observed query adds evidence to the green H_d tiles.
The tiles summarize sensitivity for each key and channel.

00:28.000 --> 00:35.200
QClip uses the H_d weights, with a small positive floor,
to score the key reconstruction error of 25 candidates.

00:35.200 --> 00:40.000
Select argmin J: the candidate with the lowest weighted error.
The selected tile remains as the other candidates fade.

00:40.000 --> 00:50.000
The selected candidate sets the quantizer.
Blue key tiles pass through Quantize once and become 2-bit codes.

00:50.000 --> 01:00.000
Store the selected key codes with FP16 scale and offset.
Keep the baseline bit allocation, storage format, and cache schedule.
